.TH REC2JSON "1" "April 2026" "GNU recutils 1.9.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rec2json \- rec to json converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rec2json
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR]... [\fI\,REC_FILE\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert rec data into JSON data.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-type\fR=\fI\,TYPE\/\fR
record set to convert; if this parameter
is omitted then the default record set is used
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-sort\fR=\fI\,FIELDS\/\fR
sort the output by the specified fields.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
print a help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert all records to JSON:

  rec2json contacts.rec

Convert only a specific record type:

  rec2json -t Task todo.rec

Sort the output by a field:

  rec2json -S Name contacts.rec

Pipe from recsel for filtered JSON output:

  recsel -e "Status = 'open'" todo.rec | rec2json
